window.EXAMS=[{"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A", "track": "tefl", "scope": "lesson", "ref": "tefl-01", "model": "A", "title": "امتحان درس TEFL 1: عالم الـ <span class=\"en\">TEFL</span> (نموذج A)", "minutes": 15, "pass_percent": 60, "items": [{"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:1", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">According to the lesson, what is the teacher's main job in the classroom?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What is the main job of the teacher in the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">حسب الدرس، إيه الوظيفة الأساسية للمدرّس في الفصل؟</div>", "o": ["To give as much information as possible in each class", "To correct every mistake immediately", "To create the conditions in which learning can take place", "To make sure students speak only English"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: more information does not mean more learning.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: معلومات أكتر مش معناها تعلم أكتر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: correcting everything can add stress.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: تصحيح كل حاجة ممكن يزوّد التوتر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the teacher sets up the room and tasks, gives instructions and guides the group, so learning can happen.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: المدرّس بيجهّز المكان والمهام ويوجّه المجموعة عشان التعلم يحصل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson does not say this is the main job.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش إن ده الدور الأساسي.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:2", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A confident adult learner suddenly becomes shy in class because she fears making mistakes in front of others. Which term describes this stress that harms acquisition?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A student is afraid of mistakes and becomes shy. What is the name for this stress?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلمة واثقة بقت فجأة خجولة في الفصل عشان خايفة تغلط قدام الناس. إيه اسم التوتر ده؟</div>", "o": ["The affective filter", "Inflection", "Diacritics", "The continuous tense"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the affective filter is stress that blocks learning and language acquisition.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الـ <span class=\"en\">affective filter</span> هو التوتر اللي بيعطّل التعلم واكتساب اللغة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: inflection means extra letters added to a word for grammar.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الـ <span class=\"en\">inflection</span> حروف بتتضاف للكلمة لأسباب قواعدية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: diacritics are small marks on letters.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الـ <span class=\"en\">diacritics</span> علامات صغيرة فوق الحروف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the continuous tense is a verb form for ongoing actions.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الـ <span class=\"en\">continuous tense</span> زمن للأفعال المستمرة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:3", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">How many forms does a regular English verb have, and what does this show about English?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">How many forms does a regular verb have? What does it show?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">كام شكل للفعل المنتظم في الإنجليزي؟ وده بيدل على إيه؟</div>", "o": ["Eight; English is heavily inflected", "Two; English has no inflection at all", "Six; English is inflected like French", "Four (look, looks, looked, looking); English is weakly inflected"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: English has far fewer forms than that.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: أشكاله أقل من كده بكتير.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: English has some inflection, but very little.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: فيه تصريف بس قليل جدًا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: French and Russian are more heavily inflected than English.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الفرنسي والروسي تصريفهم أكتر من الإنجليزي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: regular verbs have only four forms, so English has simple inflection.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الفعل المنتظم ليه أربع أشكال بس، فالتصريف في الإنجليزي بسيط.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:4", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which statement correctly describes how English verbs change with the person in the present tense?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">How do English verbs change with the person in the present tense?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إزاي الأفعال الإنجليزية بتتغير مع الشخص في المضارع؟</div>", "o": ["Every person has a different ending", "Only the third person singular usually changes: I eat, you eat, she eats", "Only the first person changes", "No verb ever changes with the person"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: that is true in more inflected languages, not English.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده بيحصل في لغات تصريفها أكتر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the only common change is third person singular (she eats).</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: التغيير الشائع الوحيد هو المفرد الغائب (she eats).</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the first person does not change.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المتكلم (I) مبيتغيرش.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: 'no verb ever' is too strong, since 'she eats' changes.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: «ولا فعل» مبالغة، لأن she eats بيتغير.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:5", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which sentence follows the most common English word order (SVO)?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which sentence has the normal English order: Subject, Verb, Object?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي جملة بتمشي على الترتيب الأشهر في الإنجليزي (فاعل، فعل، مفعول)؟</div>", "o": ["Bought I a new computer.", "A new computer I bought.", "I bought a new computer.", "I a new computer bought."], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the verb comes before the subject.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الفعل جه قبل الفاعل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the object comes first.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المفعول جه الأول.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: Subject (I), Verb (bought), Object (a new computer).</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: فاعل (I) ثم فعل (bought) ثم مفعول (a new computer).</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the verb comes at the end.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الفعل جه في الآخر.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:6", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which sentence contains a phrasal verb?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which sentence has a phrasal verb (a verb plus a small word)?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي جملة فيها <span class=\"en\">phrasal verb</span> (فعل + كلمة صغيرة)؟</div>", "o": ["They look down on cheap hotels.", "The cat sleeps on the sofa.", "She runs very quickly.", "He eats breakfast at home."], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: 'look down on' is a verb with two small words, and the meaning is not simply the sum of the parts.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: <span class=\"en\">look down on</span> فعل ومعاه كلمتين صغيرين ومعناه مش مجموع الأجزاء.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: 'sleeps' is a plain verb followed by a normal prepositional phrase.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: <span class=\"en\">sleeps</span> فعل عادي وبعده عبارة مكان.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: 'runs' is a plain verb with an adverb.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: <span class=\"en\">runs</span> فعل عادي ومعاه ظرف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: 'eats' is a plain verb with a place phrase.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: <span class=\"en\">eats</span> فعل عادي ومعاه عبارة مكان.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:7", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A Chinese learner expects that raising pitch on an English word will change its meaning. Which statement about English is correct?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A Chinese student thinks high or low pitch changes a word's meaning. What is true in English?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم صيني فاكر إن رفع النغمة على كلمة إنجليزي بيغيّر معناها. إيه الصح في الإنجليزي؟</div>", "o": ["Pitch decides the meaning of every word", "Pitch changes meaning only in questions", "English has four tones like Mandarin", "Pitch only adds emphasis or emotion; it never changes the meaning of a word"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: that describes tonal languages such as Chinese and Vietnamese.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده وصف للغات النغمية زي الصيني والفيتنامي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson does not say this.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش كده.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: English has no tones.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإنجليزي مفيهوش نغمات.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: English is not a tonal language, so pitch adds emphasis or emotion only.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الإنجليزي مش لغة نغمية، فالنغمة بتضيف تأكيد أو عاطفة بس.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:8", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A learner says 'I had a bath when the phone rang' instead of 'I was having a bath when the phone rang'. What is the most likely reason?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A student says 'I had a bath when the phone rang'. Why?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم قال <span class=\"en\">I had a bath when the phone rang</span> بدل <span class=\"en\">I was having a bath when the phone rang</span>. أغلب سبب إيه؟</div>", "o": ["His first language may not have a continuous tense", "He cannot pronounce 'th'", "His language uses an alphabet with marks", "He does not know the articles"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: many languages have no continuous tense, so learners use the simple past instead.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: لغات كتير مفيهاش زمن مستمر، فالمتعلم بيستخدم الماضي البسيط.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this error is about verb form, not sound.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الغلطة في شكل الفعل مش في النطق.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: letter marks are not related to this error.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: علامات الحروف مالهاش علاقة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: articles are not involved in this sentence.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مفيش أدوات تعريف في الجملة دي.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:9", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Most English words follow spelling patterns, yet learners find spelling hard. Why?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Most English words follow patterns. Why is spelling still hard?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أغلب الكلمات الإنجليزية ليها أنماط إملاء، ومع كده المتعلمين بيلاقوا الإملاء صعب. ليه؟</div>", "o": ["Most English words have silent letters", "English has more than 26 letters", "The words that break the patterns are some of the most common, so learners meet them first", "Spelling rules change from one teacher to another"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: silent letters appear in some words, not most.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الحروف الصامتة في بعض الكلمات مش أغلبها.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: English uses the 26-letter Latin alphabet.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإنجليزي بيستخدم الأبجدية اللاتينية 26 حرف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: common words like 'could' or 'their' break the patterns, so beginners meet the exceptions early.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: كلمات شائعة زي <span class=\"en\">could</span> و<span class=\"en\">their</span> بتكسر الأنماط، فالمبتدئ بيقابل الاستثناءات بدري.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the problem is the language, not the teacher.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المشكلة في اللغة مش في المدرّس.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:10", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which word is an exception to the rule that English has no marks on its letters?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which English word has a mark on a letter?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي كلمة إنجليزية فيها علامة فوق حرف (استثناء من إن الإنجليزي مفيهوش علامات)؟</div>", "o": ["thirteenth", "naïve", "clothes", "months"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: 'thirteenth' has no mark. It is hard to pronounce, not to write.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: <span class=\"en\">thirteenth</span> مفيهاش علامة، صعبة في النطق.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: 'naïve' is imported from French, and imported words are the main exceptions.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: <span class=\"en\">naïve</span> مستوردة من الفرنسي، والكلمات المستوردة هي الاستثناء.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: 'clothes' has no mark.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: <span class=\"en\">clothes</span> مفيهاش علامة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: 'months' has no mark.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: <span class=\"en\">months</span> مفيهاش علامة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:11", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">The English word 'alligator' comes from the Spanish 'el lagarto'. Which feature of English does this show?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">'Alligator' comes from Spanish. What does this show about English?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">كلمة <span class=\"en\">alligator</span> جاية من الإسبانية <span class=\"en\">el lagarto</span>. ده بيوضّح أي سمة في الإنجليزي؟</div>", "o": ["English has a fixed word order", "English has simple inflection", "English is a tonal language", "English is very open to words from other languages"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: word order is a different feature.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ترتيب الكلمات سمة تانية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: inflection is about word endings.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التصريف عن نهايات الكلمات.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: English is not tonal.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإنجليزي مش نغمي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: English takes many words from other languages.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الإنجليزي بيستعير كلمات كتير من لغات تانية.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}, {"id": "tefl-01-lesson-A:12", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which group of learners will probably find the articles 'a', 'an' and 'the' most difficult?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Who will find 'a', 'an' and 'the' most difficult?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي متعلمين غالبًا هيلاقوا <span class=\"en\">a</span> و<span class=\"en\">an</span> و<span class=\"en\">the</span> أصعب حاجة؟</div>", "o": ["Learners whose first language has many articles", "Learners whose first language has no articles", "Learners who already know the Latin alphabet", "Learners who speak a language with a fixed word order"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: they already have the idea of articles, so it is easier.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: عندهم فكرة الأدوات أصلًا، فأسهل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: when the first language has no articles, the idea is new and hard.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: لو لغتهم الأولى مفيهاش أدوات تعريف، الفكرة جديدة وصعبة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the alphabet is not related to articles.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الأبجدية مالهاش علاقة بالأدوات.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: word order is not related to articles.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ترتيب الكلمات مالوش علاقة بالأدوات.</div>"], "l": "tefl-01"}]}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A", "track": "tefl", "scope": "lesson", "ref": "tefl-02", "model": "A", "title": "امتحان درس TEFL 2: اللغة الأولى لطلابك (نموذج A)", "minutes": 18, "pass_percent": 60, "items": [{"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:1", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A Spanish-speaking learner says 'The cars are a hassle' when making a general statement. Which feature of Spanish most likely explains the extra article?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A Spanish student says 'The cars are a hassle' about cars in general. Why?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم إسباني قال <span class=\"en\">The cars are a hassle</span> وهو بيتكلم عن العربيات عمومًا. إيه السبب الأرجح؟</div>", "o": ["Spanish has no articles at all", "Spanish adjectives come after the noun", "Spanish drops the subject pronoun", "Spanish uses 'the' in places where English uses no article"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish has articles (el, la, los).</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني فيه أدوات تعريف (el, la, los).</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is about adjective position, which is not shown here.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده عن ترتيب الصفة ومش ظاهر هنا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: pronoun dropping is a different error.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: حذف الضمير غلطة تانية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: Spanish says 'Los coches son una molestia', so the article is added where English uses none.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الإسباني بيقول <span class=\"en\">Los coches son una molestia</span> فبيضيف أداة تعريف في مكان الإنجليزي مبيحطش فيه.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:2", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Spanish learners often confuse 'ship' and 'sheep'. Which explanation from the lesson is correct?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Spanish students mix up 'ship' and 'sheep'. Why?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">المتعلمين الإسبان بيخلطوا بين <span class=\"en\">ship</span> و<span class=\"en\">sheep</span>. إيه التفسير الصح؟</div>", "o": ["Spanish has more vowel sounds than English", "Spanish words are never spelled as they sound", "Spanish has fewer vowel sounds and vowel length is not important, so they cannot hear the difference first", "Spanish learners cannot pronounce any consonants"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish has fewer vowel sounds than English.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني أصواته المتحركة أقل من الإنجليزي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: in Spanish, spelling and sound match closely.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: في الإسباني الإملاء والنطق متطابقين تقريبًا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: they first cannot hear the difference, and then cannot say it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: أول حاجة مبيسمعوش الفرق، وبعدين مبيعرفوش ينطقوه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the problem here is vowels, not all consonants.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المشكلة في المتحركة مش كل الحروف الساكنة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:3", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A Spanish speaker says 'I went to eschool in Barcelona'. What is the cause?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why does a Spanish student say 'eschool'?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم إسباني قال <span class=\"en\">I went to eschool</span>. إيه السبب؟</div>", "o": ["He confuses v and b", "He drops the final consonant", "He uses a tonal pattern", "Spanish words do not start with an s sound before another consonant, so he adds an e sound"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: v and b confusion is a different problem.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: لخبطة v وb مشكلة تانية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: dropping final consonants is more typical of Chinese learners.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: حذف الحرف الأخير أقرب لمتعلمين صينيين.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish is not tonal.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني مش نغمي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the learner adds an 'e' before 's' + consonant, as in 'Espain'.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: بيضيف صوت <span class=\"en\">e</span> قبل <span class=\"en\">s</span> + حرف ساكن زي <span class=\"en\">Espain</span>.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:4", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A Spanish-speaking learner reads 'The Beatles were bigger than Elvis' with every syllable at the same length. Which statement fits?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A Spanish student says every syllable with the same time. Why does this sound strange in English?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم إسباني بينطق كل مقطع بنفس الزمن. ليه ده بيبان غريب في الإنجليزي؟</div>", "o": ["Spanish is stress-timed and English is syllable-timed", "Spanish is syllable-timed and English is stress-timed, so he sounds flat", "Both languages are stress-timed", "Both languages are syllable-timed"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this reverses the two languages.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده عكس الحقيقة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: English squashes small syllables between stressed beats, but the learner gives each equal time.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الإنجليزي بيضغط المقاطع الصغيرة بين النبرات، والمتعلم بيدي كل مقطع زمن متساوي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish is syllable-timed.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني زمنه مقطعي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: English is stress-timed.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإنجليزي زمنه نبري.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:5", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A Spanish speaker answers 'Is Carlos here?' with 'Yes. Is here.' Which explanation fits?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A Spanish student says 'Is here' without a subject. Why?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم إسباني رد <span class=\"en\">Yes. Is here.</span> من غير فاعل. ليه؟</div>", "o": ["Spanish has no verbs", "In Spanish, speakers often drop the subject pronoun because the verb ending shows who is meant", "Spanish always puts the subject last", "Spanish has no word for 'here'"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish has verbs.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني فيه أفعال.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the verb ending carries the information, and the habit moves into English.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: نهاية الفعل بتوضح الفاعل، والعادة دي بتنتقل للإنجليزي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the problem is a missing pronoun, not word order.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المشكلة ضمير ناقص مش ترتيب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not what the lesson says.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش كده.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:6", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why are prepositions especially difficult for Spanish learners of English?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why are English prepositions hard for Spanish students?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه حروف الجر في الإنجليزي صعبة على المتعلمين الإسبان؟</div>", "o": ["Most have several meanings and are short, so they are hard to hear, and L1 words like 'por' do not match one English word", "English has only a few prepositions", "Spanish has no prepositions", "They are always stressed in English"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: 'por' can be by, for, during or through, and English prepositions are short and quick in speech.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: <span class=\"en\">por</span> ممكن تكون <span class=\"en\">by</span> أو <span class=\"en\">for</span> أو <span class=\"en\">during</span> أو <span class=\"en\">through</span>، وحروف الجر الإنجليزي قصيرة وسريعة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: English has many prepositions, more than many languages.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإنجليزي فيه حروف جر كتير.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish has prepositions (like 'por').</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني فيه حروف جر زي <span class=\"en\">por</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: they are usually short and weak, not stressed.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: غالبًا قصيرة وضعيفة مش منبورة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:7", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A Spanish learner writes 'the book of the boy' instead of 'the boy's book'. What is the most likely reason?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A Spanish student says 'the book of the boy'. Why?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم إسباني كتب <span class=\"en\">the book of the boy</span> بدل <span class=\"en\">the boy's book</span>. أغلب سبب إيه؟</div>", "o": ["Spanish uses only the 'of' construction for possession", "Spanish has no nouns", "Spanish uses the apostrophe for everything", "Spanish adjectives come before the noun"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: Spanish has no possessive apostrophe, so learners use the 'of' form.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الإسباني مفيهوش علامة الملكية، فالمتعلم بيستخدم <span class=\"en\">of</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish has nouns.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني فيه أسماء.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish does not use the possessive apostrophe.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني مبيستخدمش الفاصلة العليا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: adjective position is not related to this error.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مكان الصفة مالوش علاقة بالغلطة دي.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:8", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which advantage do Spanish learners of English have over Chinese learners?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Spanish students have one big advantage over Chinese students. What is it?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه ميزة المتعلمين الإسبان على الصينيين؟</div>", "o": ["They already know pinyin", "They share many cognates with English", "Their language is stress-timed", "Their language has no articles"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: pinyin helps some Chinese learners, not Spanish ones.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الـ <span class=\"en\">pinyin</span> بيفيد بعض الصينيين مش الإسبان.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: cognates are words with a shared history, so they look and mean alike. Chinese has very few.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الـ <span class=\"en\">cognates</span> كلمات بتشبه بعض في الشكل والمعنى. الصيني مفيهوش تقريبًا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish is syllable-timed.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني زمنه مقطعي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish has articles.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني فيه أدوات تعريف.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:9", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">How does the Chinese writing system differ from English, and why is pinyin not a complete solution?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">How is Chinese writing different from English? Why does pinyin not solve everything?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">الكتابة الصينية بتختلف عن الإنجليزي إزاي؟ وليه <span class=\"en\">pinyin</span> مش حل كامل؟</div>", "o": ["Chinese is logographic (symbols stand for words); pinyin is phonetic, but its letter-sound match differs from English", "Chinese is alphabetic like English; pinyin is a logographic system", "Chinese has no writing system; pinyin replaces it", "Chinese uses the Greek alphabet; pinyin is identical to English spelling"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: pinyin uses Latin letters but with its own sound values, so it can mislead learners.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الـ <span class=\"en\">pinyin</span> بحروف لاتينية بس بقيم صوتية مختلفة، فممكن يضلل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Chinese is logographic, not alphabetic.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الصيني <span class=\"en\">logographic</span> مش أبجدي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Chinese has a writing system.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الصيني ليه نظام كتابة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Chinese does not use the Greek alphabet.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الصيني مبيستخدمش الأبجدية اليونانية.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:10", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Chinese is an uninflected language. How does this affect Chinese learners of English?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Chinese words do not change form. How is this a problem in English?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">الصيني لغة بلا تصريف. ده بيأثر إزاي على المتعلم الصيني في الإنجليزي؟</div>", "o": ["They find the word order of English impossible", "They cannot learn any vocabulary", "They automatically use all verb forms correctly", "Verb changes like eat, eats, ate, eaten and helping verbs are new to them, since meaning comes from word order and context in Chinese"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the problem is changing forms, not word order.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المشكلة في تغيير الأشكال مش الترتيب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: vocabulary is not the issue.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المفردات مش هي المشكلة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says the opposite.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول العكس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: English shows meaning with helping verbs and verb changes, which Chinese does not do.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الإنجليزي بيعبّر بالأفعال المساعدة وتغيّر الفعل، والصيني مبيعملش كده.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:11", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A Chinese learner often drops the last consonant of English words. What explains this?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A Chinese student drops the last sound of words. Why?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم صيني بيحذف آخر حرف ساكن في الكلمات الإنجليزية. ليه؟</div>", "o": ["Mandarin has no consonants", "Mandarin words always end with a vowel", "Mandarin allows only three consonant sounds at the end of a syllable", "Chinese learners dislike consonants"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Mandarin has consonants.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الماندرين فيه حروف ساكنة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is too general.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: تعميم زيادة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: English words ending with other sounds are very hard, so the final consonant is dropped.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الكلمات اللي بتنتهي بأصوات تانية صعبة جدًا، فبيحذف الحرف الأخير.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not a reason.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش سبب.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:12", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A Chinese learner says 'He sad' and 'I like dog'. Which two features of Chinese explain these errors?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A Chinese student says 'He sad' and 'I like dog'. Why?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم صيني قال <span class=\"en\">He sad</span> و<span class=\"en\">I like dog</span>. إيه سمتين في الصيني بيفسّروا الأخطاء دي؟</div>", "o": ["Chinese has no verb 'to be' before adjectives and no articles", "Chinese has too many articles and always uses 'to be'", "Chinese has gender endings", "Chinese uses only the past tense"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the learner drops 'to be' before an adjective and drops the article.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: بيحذف <span class=\"en\">to be</span> قبل الصفة وبيحذف أداة التعريف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Chinese has no articles.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الصيني مفيهوش أدوات تعريف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: gender endings are a Spanish feature.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: نهايات الجنس سمة إسبانية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not in the lesson.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش في الدرس.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}, {"id": "tefl-02-lesson-A:13", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What is the main message of the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What is the big idea of the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه الفكرة الكبيرة في الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Spanish and Chinese students are the same", "You must speak your students' language fluently", "Every language is different, so learn about your students' first language from day 1", "Individual students never differ from the general observations"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson compares them as different.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقارن بينهم كمختلفين.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: you do not need to speak or write their language.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش لازم تتكلم أو تكتب لغتهم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: knowing key differences helps you choose a teaching strategy.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: معرفة الفروق الأساسية بتساعدك تختار استراتيجية التدريس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says individual students can be different.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول إن الأفراد ممكن يختلفوا.</div>"], "l": "tefl-02"}]}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A", "track": "tefl", "scope": "lesson", "ref": "tefl-03", "model": "A", "title": "امتحان درس TEFL 3: اللغة الأولى والثانية في الفصل (نموذج A)", "minutes": 18, "pass_percent": 60, "items": [{"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:1", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A Spanish speaker is learning English. Which labels are correct?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A Spanish speaker learns English. What are L1 and L2 for this person?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متحدث إسباني بيتعلم إنجليزي. إيه الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> وإيه الـ <span class=\"en\">L2</span> بالنسبة له؟</div>", "o": ["L1 is Spanish and L2 is English", "L1 is English and L2 is Spanish", "Both are L1", "Both are L2"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: L1 is the first (native) language and L2 is the new language being learned.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> هي اللغة الأولى (الأم) والـ <span class=\"en\">L2</span> هي اللغة الجديدة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this reverses the labels.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده عكس التسميات.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: English is not his native language.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإنجليزي مش لغته الأم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Spanish is his first language, so it is his L1.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإسباني لغته الأولى يعني <span class=\"en\">L1</span>.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:2", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">In the story about the aircraft carrier, why did the teachers explain the passage in the learners' L1?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">In the story, why did the teachers use the students' own language?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">في قصة حاملة الطائرات، ليه المدرّسين شرحوا الفقرة بلغة المتعلمين الأولى؟</div>", "o": ["The learners refused to read English", "The teachers did not know English well", "There was no passage to read", "The idea was too complex to explain in English without a long period of confusion"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson does not say this.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش كده.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the issue was the concept, not the teachers' English.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المشكلة في الفكرة مش لغة المدرّسين.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the passage was needed for language and continuity.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الفقرة كانت مطلوبة للغة والاستمرارية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the learners had never seen a big ship, so the concept needed a clear L1 explanation.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: المتعلمين عمرهم ما شافوا سفينة كبيرة، فالفكرة محتاجة شرح واضح بلغتهم.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:3", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">For most of the past century, which view about L1 in the L2 classroom was winning, and what was its main argument?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">For many years, what did most teachers think about L1 in class?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">في أغلب القرن الماضي، أي رأي عن استخدام الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> في فصل الـ <span class=\"en\">L2</span> كان هو الغالب؟ وإيه حجته؟</div>", "o": ["In favour of L1: it should be used for all explanations", "Against L1: it is too expensive", "In favour of L1: it makes lessons shorter", "Against L1: avoiding it gives maximum classroom time for studying the L2"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the winning side was against L1.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الجانب الغالب كان ضد استخدام الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: cost was not the argument.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التكلفة مش الحجة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the winning side was against L1.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الجانب الغالب كان ضد الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: 'Use English only' was a commonly heard order.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: كان شائع الأمر <span class=\"en\">Use English only</span>.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:4", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What position does the lesson recommend today about the students' L1?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What does the lesson say about L1 now?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه الموقف اللي بيوصي بيه الدرس النهارده من الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> عند الطلاب؟</div>", "o": ["Treat it as another classroom resource and use it with good judgment", "Ban it completely", "Use it as the main language of every lesson", "Use it only for beginners at the end of a course"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: use the L1 judiciously to reach certain goals.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: استخدم الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> بحُسن تقدير لتحقيق أهداف معينة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says the pendulum has swung back.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول إن البندول رجع.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: use it only in specific circumstances.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: استخدمه في ظروف محددة بس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson does not say this.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش كده.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:5", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher quickly mentions in Thai that English has articles, which Thai does not, before an activity. Which reason for using L1 is this?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A teacher tells Thai students in Thai that English has articles. Why is this useful?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّس قال للطلاب التايلانديين بلغتهم إن الإنجليزي فيه أدوات تعريف وهي مش موجودة في التايلاندي. ده أي سبب لاستخدام الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span>؟</div>", "o": ["To show that the teacher dislikes English", "To clarify anticipated problems before students make mistakes", "To discipline the class", "To replace the lesson"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: that is not a reason in the lesson.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش سبب في الدرس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: a short L1 reference shows the difference early, instead of waiting for errors.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: إشارة قصيرة بالـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> بتوضح الفرق بدري بدل ما تستنى الأخطاء.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not a disciplinary use.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش استخدام تأديبي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: it supports the lesson, not replaces it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: بيدعم الدرس مش بيستبدله.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:6", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which situation best fits the lesson's idea of using L1 to save time?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">When is L1 a good way to save time?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي موقف بيناسب فكرة استخدام الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> لتوفير الوقت؟</div>", "o": ["Translating every sentence in the lesson", "Teaching the whole lesson in L1", "Giving the instructions for an activity on a specific occasion", "Never explaining instructions"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: constant translation removes L2 time.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الترجمة المستمرة بتضيّع وقت الـ <span class=\"en\">L2</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson recommends using L1 only in specific cases.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيوصي بالاستخدام المحدد.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: translation is time-efficient, but only on specific occasions.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الترجمة بتوفر وقت، لكن في مناسبات محددة بس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: unclear instructions waste time.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التعليمات الغامضة بتضيّع وقت.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:7", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why does the lesson suggest using L1 for disciplinary measures?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why can L1 help with discipline?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه الدرس بيقترح استخدام الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> في الانضباط؟</div>", "o": ["It makes the lesson longer", "It is a punishment", "It shows you do not speak English", "It makes students sit up and listen, and shows that what you say is real"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the purpose is not length.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الهدف مش الطول.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: it is not a punishment.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش عقاب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not what the lesson says.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش كده.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the L1 shows that the statement is real, not pretend.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> بيبيّن إن كلامك حقيقي مش تمثيل.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:8", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which action shows the learners that you care, according to the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">How can you show students that you care?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي تصرف بيوضّح للمتعلمين إنك مهتم، حسب الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Never speaking their language", "Learning a little of their language, even in a short time", "Giving them more homework", "Correcting every mistake"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this shows the opposite.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده بيوضّح العكس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the effort to learn a bit of their language will be appreciated.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: المجهود إنك تتعلم حاجة من لغتهم بيتقدّر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: homework is not related.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الواجب مالوش علاقة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: heavy correction can demotivate.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التصحيح الكتير ممكن يحبط.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:9", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which statement describes a child learning L1?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">How does a child learn her first language?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي عبارة بتوصف طفل بيتعلم لغته الأولى؟</div>", "o": ["She learns mostly in a classroom with controlled practice", "She gets little attention from adults", "She is immersed in the language and is motivated to communicate, and she is not often corrected", "She is corrected for accuracy every day"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this describes the L2 learner.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده وصف متعلم الـ <span class=\"en\">L2</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: she gets a lot of attention.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: بياخد اهتمام كتير.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the child hears the language all the time, and adults praise her.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الطفل بيسمع اللغة طول الوقت والكبار بيشجعوه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: she is not often corrected.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش بيتصحح كتير.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:10", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which statement about L2 learners is supported by the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which sentence about L2 learners is true?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي عبارة عن متعلمي الـ <span class=\"en\">L2</span> بيدعمها الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["They are immersed in English all day", "They never need praise", "They often get limited exposure outside the classroom and regular correction, which can demotivate some", "They receive more attention than a child"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this describes an L1 child.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده وصف طفل الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says to praise good behaviour.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول امدح السلوك الجيد.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: exposure is mostly through teaching, and frequent correction can be demotivating.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: التعرض في الغالب بيكون عن طريق التدريس، والتصحيح المستمر ممكن يحبط.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: they receive limited attention.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: بياخدوا اهتمام محدود.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:11", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher notices a student making a clear effort and showing good specific behaviour. What does the lesson suggest?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A student behaves very well. What should the teacher do?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّس لاحظ طالب بيبذل مجهود وسلوكه كويس بشكل محدد. إيه اللي بيقترحه الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Praise the student", "Ignore it so others do not feel bad", "Correct the student's accent", "Switch fully to L1"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: teachers vary in praise, so deliberately praise good, specific behaviour.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: المدرّسين بيختلفوا في المديح، فامدح السلوك الجيد المحدد قصدًا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: praise helps motivation.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المديح بيساعد الدافعية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is unrelated.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مالوش علاقة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not what the lesson says.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش كده.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}, {"id": "tefl-03-lesson-A:12", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which of the following is NOT one of the reasons for using L1 given in the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which one is NOT a reason for using L1?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي سبب مما يلي مش من أسباب استخدام الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> اللي ذكرها الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["To clarify meaning", "To replace English completely whenever students find a task difficult", "To show that languages share similarities", "To give feedback in the student's own language"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: clarifying meaning is reason 1.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: توضيح المعنى هو السبب 1.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the lesson says to use L1 judiciously, not as a replacement.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الدرس بيقول استخدم الـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> بحُسن تقدير مش كبديل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: showing similarities is reason 3.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: إظهار التشابهات هو السبب 3.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: feedback in L1 adds weight (reason 6).</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التغذية الراجعة بالـ <span class=\"en\">L1</span> السبب 6.</div>"], "l": "tefl-03"}]}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A", "track": "tefl", "scope": "lesson", "ref": "tefl-04", "model": "A", "title": "امتحان درس TEFL 4: إيه اللي بيأثر على تعلم اللغة الثانية؟ (نموذج A)", "minutes": 20, "pass_percent": 60, "items": [{"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:1", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A learner who was energetic and engaged last week has become withdrawn and inattentive today. Which interpretation is most consistent with the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Last week a student was active. Today he is quiet and not focused. What is the best explanation?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">طالب كان نشيط ومركّز الأسبوع اللي فات، النهارده ساكت ومشتّت. أنسب تفسير إيه؟</div>", "o": ["His motivation can change from day to day because of things happening in his life, so empathy is part of the job.", "His intellect has dropped, so he needs easier material.", "His learning style no longer matches, so you should switch every activity.", "Motivation is a fixed trait, so a one-off dip should simply be ignored."], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the whole person comes to class. Problems at home can lower motivation from day to day.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الشخص كله بييجي الفصل، والمشاكل الشخصية بتأثر على الدافعية من يوم للتاني.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: intellect does not change in one week. This is a personal situation.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الذكاء مش بيتغير في أسبوع، والمشكلة هنا ظرف شخصي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: there is no sign that learning style is the cause. Changing everything is too much.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مفيش دليل إن الأسلوب هو السبب، وتغيير كل حاجة مبالغة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: motivation changes. If you ignore it, you miss a chance to help.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدافعية بتتغير، وتجاهلها بيضيّع فرصة تساعد الطالب.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:2", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which of the following learners most clearly illustrates extrinsic motivation?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which student is the best example of extrinsic motivation?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي متعلم هو أوضح مثال على الدافعية الخارجية (<span class=\"en\">extrinsic</span>)؟</div>", "o": ["A learner who studies English because she enjoys how the language sounds.", "A learner who studies English because solving grammar puzzles is fun.", "A learner who studies English because he finds the culture interesting for its own sake.", "A learner who studies English only to qualify for a salary bonus."], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: she learns for the pleasure of it. That is intrinsic motivation.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده تعلم عشان المتعة، يعني دافعية داخلية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: enjoying the learning itself is intrinsic motivation.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الاستمتاع بالتعلم نفسه دافعية داخلية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: interest in the culture for its own sake is intrinsic motivation.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الاهتمام بالثقافة لذاتها دافعية داخلية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: extrinsic motivation comes from a goal or reward outside learning itself.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الدافعية الخارجية بتيجي من هدف أو مكافأة برّه التعلم نفسه.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:3", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">You are teaching adults who were schooled in a formal, authoritarian system, and they appear perplexed when you address them by first name and allow them to move around the room. What is the most appropriate initial response?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Your adult students come from a strict, formal school system. They look confused when you use first names and let them move. What should you do first?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">بتدرّس لكبار جاين من نظام مدرسي رسمي وصارم. بيبصوا مستغربين لما بتناديهم بالأسماء الأولى وتسيبهم يتحركوا. أفضل خطوة أولى إيه؟</div>", "o": ["Keep your informal style, since they will adapt in time.", "Switch to a strict, formal style at once to match their past.", "Assume they dislike the course and report low motivation.", "Ask them how they were taught before and how they prefer to learn now."], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: you ignore their expectations, and that affects their learning.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: كده بتتجاهل توقعاتهم، وده بيأثر على تعلمهم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: you force a style without asking, and they may not want it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: بتفرض أسلوب من غير ما تسأل، وممكن ميكونوش عايزينه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is a guess without proof. Being confused means different expectations, not low motivation.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: افتراض من غير دليل، والاستغراب معناه اختلاف توقعات مش قلة دافع.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: you cannot guess. Ask them. Some may like the change and some may not.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: مينفعش تخمّن، فبتسأل. ممكن يرحبوا بالتغيير وممكن لأ.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:4", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A learner concludes that her teacher is poorly prepared because the activities appear unordered and errors are corrected only intermittently. Which influence on L2 learning does this illustrate?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A student thinks her teacher is lazy. Activities come in a random order, and mistakes are corrected only sometimes. Which influence on L2 learning is this?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلمة شايفة إن مدرّسها كسلان لأن الأنشطة بتيجي بترتيب عشوائي والأخطاء بتتصحح كل فين وفين. ده أي عامل من العوامل المؤثرة على تعلم الـ <span class=\"en\">L2</span>؟</div>", "o": ["Her degree of intellect.", "Her expectation about the pattern of classroom activity.", "Her proficiency in her first language.", "Her motivation to find a job."], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the problem is expectation, not intelligence.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المشكلة هنا توقع مش ذكاء.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: some learners expect a clear order and steady correction. If the teacher does not do this, they think the teacher is not prepared.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: بعض المتعلمين بيتوقعوا ترتيب واضح وتصحيح مستمر، ولو المدرّس مش كده يشوفوه مش مجهّز.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: her first language does not explain how she judges the activities.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: اللغة الأولى مالهاش علاقة بحكمها على ترتيب الأنشطة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the situation is not about her job goal.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الموقف مش عن الهدف الوظيفي.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:5", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher raised in a culture that prizes self-reliance and individual advancement designs every task around personal goals, presuming that the class shares them. What is the principal risk of this approach?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A teacher values independence and personal success. Every task is about individual goals, and the teacher thinks the class wants the same. What is the main risk?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّس جاي من ثقافة بتقدّر الاعتماد على النفس والتقدم الشخصي، بيبني كل مهمة على أهداف فردية وبيفترض إن الفصل عايز نفس الحاجة. أكبر خطر إيه؟</div>", "o": ["The teacher's own expectations may clash with learners who do not share those goals.", "The learners will have too little L1 proficiency.", "The learners will use too many cognitive strategies.", "The tasks will be too direct in communication style."], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the teacher's own behaviour and culture are one of the 12 influences. Unspoken assumptions can clash with the learners' expectations.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: سلوك المدرّس وافتراضاته الثقافية من العوامل الـ 12، والافتراضات الصامتة بتتصادم مع توقعات المتعلمين.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: individual tasks are not linked to L1 level.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مفيش علاقة بين المهام الفردية وإجادة اللغة الأولى.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: cognitive strategies are not the problem here.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الاستراتيجيات المعرفية مش المشكلة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: communication style is not the risk in this case.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: أسلوب التواصل مش هو موضوع الخطر هنا.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:6", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">When asked a yes/no question, a learner responds with a brief anecdote that implies the answer without ever stating it. Which communication style does this reflect, and what does it typically signify?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A learner answers a yes/no question with a short story that only hints at the answer. Which style is it, and what does it often mean?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم بيرد على سؤال نعم/لأ بحكاية قصيرة بتلمّح للإجابة ومبيقولش نعم ولا لأ. ده أي أسلوب تواصل، وبيدل على إيه غالبًا؟</div>", "o": ["Direct style, usually meant as honesty.", "Indirect style, usually meant as politeness and respect.", "Indirect style, usually a sign of weak L2 proficiency.", "Person-focused style, usually a sign of anger."], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: direct style says things straight, with no hints.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الأسلوب المباشر بيقول الكلام على طول من غير لف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: indirect style gives meaning by hints and stories. The speaker is usually polite, not weak.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الأسلوب غير المباشر بيوصّل المعنى بالتلميح والحكايات، وصاحبه غالبًا مؤدب مش عاجز.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: do not treat this as a language problem. It is a communication choice.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ميتاخدش على إنه مشكلة لغة، ده اختيار تواصل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: person-focused style is a different topic and has nothing to do with anger.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التركيز على الشخص موضوع تاني، ومالوش علاقة بالغضب.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:7", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">During a debate, Karim states: 'I disagree with your argument, Sara, but I think you are a great classmate.' Which communication style does Karim exemplify?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">In a debate, Karim says: 'I disagree with your argument, Sara, but I think you are a great classmate.' Which style is this?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">في مناظرة، كريم قال: «أنا مش موافق على حجتك يا سارة، بس شايفك زميلة ممتازة». كريم بيستخدم أي أسلوب؟</div>", "o": ["Idea-focused: the idea and the person are separate.", "Person-focused: disagreement is handled carefully because it hurts feelings.", "Indirect: he avoids saying what he means.", "Direct and person-focused at the same time."], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: he disagrees openly with the idea, and does not see it as an attack on the person.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: اختلف مع الفكرة مفتوحًا من غير ما يعتبره هجوم شخصي، وده أسلوب الفكرة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this would be true if the disagreement felt like an attack on the person.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده كان هيبقى لو الخلاف مع الفكرة اتحس كهجوم على الشخص.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Karim said clearly what he meant.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: كريم قال قصده بوضوح.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: direct/indirect and idea/person are different pairs. He is not person-focused here.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مباشر وفكرة أزواج مختلفة، ومينفعش يكون بيركّز على الشخص هنا.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:8", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What explains the tendency of a person-focused learner to avoid open disagreement in class discussion?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why does a person-focused learner usually avoid open disagreement in class?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه المتعلم اللي بيركّز على الشخص (<span class=\"en\">person-focused</span>) غالبًا بيتجنب الخلاف المفتوح في الفصل؟</div>", "o": ["Disagreeing with an idea feels like attacking the person.", "Person-focused learners never have opinions.", "They believe being direct is dishonest.", "They lack the vocabulary to disagree."], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the idea and the person are not separate, so disagreement feels like an attack and is handled carefully.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الفكرة والشخص مش منفصلين، فبيتعامل مع الخلاف بحذر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: they do have opinions. They express them differently.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: عنده آراء، بس طريقة التعبير مختلفة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: that describes the indirect style, not the person-focused style.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده وصف للأسلوب غير المباشر مش لأسلوب الشخص.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the reason is cultural, not about vocabulary.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: السبب ثقافي مش لغوي.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:9", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Your class includes direct and indirect communicators as well as idea-focused and person-focused learners, and friction is emerging. What is the teacher's appropriate role?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Your class has direct, indirect, idea-focused and person-focused learners, and there is tension. What is your role?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">فصلك فيه متعلمين مباشرين وغير مباشرين، وبعضهم بيركّز على الفكرة وبعضهم على الشخص، والتوتر بدأ. دورك إيه؟</div>", "o": ["Teach everyone the direct, idea-focused style so the class is consistent.", "Find a workable balance and a solution, without trying to change anyone's cultural ways.", "Avoid group work and discussion completely.", "Ask the learners who disagree most to leave the activity."], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: you would be forcing one culture on the others.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: كده بتفرض ثقافة على الباقي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: it is not your job to change people's culture. Your job is to find a solution.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: مش دورك تغيّر طرق الناس الثقافية، دورك تلاقي حل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: you avoid the problem and lose learning time.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: بتهرب من المشكلة وبتخسر التعلم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: you punish difference instead of managing it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: بتعاقب الاختلاف بدل ما تديره.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:10", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which description best characterises a more proficient user of learning strategies?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which description fits a MORE proficient strategy user?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي وصف بيناسب مستخدم استراتيجيات أكفأ؟</div>", "o": ["Uses one favourite strategy every time because it is reliable.", "Uses a wide range of strategies in many situations, matches them to the task, and can explain why.", "Uses many strategies at random without choosing for the task.", "Avoids cognitive strategies such as translating and analysing."], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: relying on only one strategy is a sign of limits.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الاعتماد على واحدة بس علامة محدودية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: more proficient learners use more strategies, fitted to the task, and can explain their choices.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الأكفأ بيستخدم مدى أوسع، ومناسب للمهمة، وبيقدر يشرح اختياراته.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: strategies must fit the task. Random use is not effective.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الاستراتيجيات لازم تتناسب مع المهمة، مش عشوائي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: proficient learners do use them, for example translating and analysing.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الأكفأ بيستخدمها فعلًا، زي الترجمة والتحليل.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:11", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which of the following is a valid method of establishing which strategies a learner employs?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">How can you find out which strategies a learner uses?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إزاي تعرف المتعلم بيستخدم أي استراتيجيات؟</div>", "o": ["Counting how many words are on his vocabulary list.", "Checking only his attendance record.", "Asking the learner to think aloud while doing a task.", "Timing how fast he reads one page."], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: vocabulary size does not show how a learner learns.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: حجم المفردات مش بيقول إزاي بيتعلم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: attendance has nothing to do with strategies.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الحضور مالوش علاقة بالاستراتيجيات.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: diaries, think-aloud, observation and surveys are ways to assess strategies.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: اليوميات والتفكير بصوت عالي والملاحظة والاستبيانات طرق لتقييم الاستراتيجيات.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: speed does not show the strategy.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: السرعة لا تكشف الاستراتيجية.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:12", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A learner cannot recall the word 'screwdriver' and instead says 'the tool you use to turn small metal things'. Which speaking strategy is being used?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A learner forgets the word 'screwdriver' and says 'the tool you use to turn small metal things'. Which speaking strategy is this?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلم نسي كلمة <span class=\"en\">screwdriver</span> وقال «الأداة اللي بتلف بيها حاجات معدنية صغيرة». ده أي استراتيجية كلام؟</div>", "o": ["Inference.", "Deduction.", "Circumlocution.", "Self-monitoring."], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: inference means working out meaning from clues. That is not what happens here.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الاستنتاج معناه تطلع المعنى من القرائن، وده مش اللي حصل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: deduction is a reading and writing strategy, not a speaking one.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الاستدلال استراتيجية قراءة وكتابة مش كلام.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: circumlocution means talking around a word you do not know.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: بتتكلم حوالين الكلمة اللي مش عارفها.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: self-monitoring means checking your own speech. It does not replace a missing word.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مراقبة النفس إنك تراجع كلامك، ومش بتعوّض كلمة ناقصة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:13", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which set contains the strategies that the lesson associates with L2 reading?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which set is the group of strategies for L2 reading in the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي مجموعة هي استراتيجيات القراءة (<span class=\"en\">reading</span>) في الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Planning, self-monitoring, deduction, substitution.", "Risk-taking, paraphrasing, circumlocution, self-evaluation.", "Elaboration, inference, selective attention, self-monitoring.", "Reading aloud, guessing, deduction, summarising."], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is the writing set.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مجموعة الكتابة (<span class=\"en\">writing</span>).</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is the speaking set.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مجموعة الكلام (<span class=\"en\">speaking</span>).</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is the listening set.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مجموعة الاستماع (<span class=\"en\">listening</span>).</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this is the reading set.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: دي مجموعة القراءة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:14", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">In a mixed-sex class, female students appear reluctant to contribute, and some male students are also hesitant when invited. Which response is most consistent with the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">In a mixed class, women seem unwilling to speak, and some men also feel uncomfortable when you ask them. What approach fits the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">في فصل مختلط، الطالبات بيبان عليهم التردد إنهم يتكلموا، وبعض الرجال كمان مش مرتاحين لما بتدعوهم. أنسب نهج من الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Treat it as low intellect and give them simpler tasks.", "Ignore it, because participation is not related to culture.", "Remember that social roles can discourage participation in mixed groups, and keep reflecting on how you invite people to speak.", "Call on them every time until they get used to it."], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: linking silence to low intelligence is a wrong assumption.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ربط التردد بالذكاء افتراض غلط.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: culture and social roles do affect participation.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الثقافة والأدوار الاجتماعية بتأثر فعلًا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the lesson asks you to keep reflecting on how you invite people to speak. Do not judge ability.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الدرس بيطلب منك تراجع باستمرار، مش تحكم على القدرة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: forcing people can increase anxiety.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الإجبار ممكن يزوّد القلق.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:15", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Two learners have equivalent English proficiency, but one has a strong command of her first language, including its grammar and structure. What does the lesson suggest about her position?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Two learners know the same amount of English. One is very strong in her first language and understands its grammar. What does the lesson say about her?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">متعلمين اتنين بيعرفوا نفس القدر من الإنجليزي، بس واحدة منهم قوية جدًا في لغتها الأولى وفاهمة قواعدها وبنيتها. إيه رأي الدرس فيها؟</div>", "o": ["She will always learn faster than anyone with better motivation.", "She is at a disadvantage, because L1 knowledge blocks L2.", "She has a great head start over others.", "L1 proficiency has no effect on L2 learning."], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: 'always' is too strong. This is only one of the 12 influences.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: «دايمًا» مبالغة، ده عامل واحد من 12.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson treats it as an advantage, not a problem.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيعتبرها ميزة مش عائق.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: strong L1 proficiency (grammar, structure) gives a head start.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الإجادة في الـ L1 (القواعد والبنية) بتدي أفضلية في البداية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson lists it as an influence on L2 learning.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيذكرها كعامل مؤثر.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}, {"id": "tefl-04-lesson-A:16", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which of the following claims about learning strategies is supported by the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which claim about strategies does the lesson support?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي ادعاء عن الاستراتيجيات بيدعمه الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["The same strategy set works best for every task and every learner.", "Strategy use is unrelated to proficiency.", "Teachers should avoid teaching strategies, because good learners find them alone.", "Combining strategies often has more impact than relying on a single one."], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: strategies must fit the task and the learner.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الاستراتيجية لازم تتناسب مع المهمة والمتعلم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: more proficient learners use a wider range.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الأكفأ بيستخدموا مدى أوسع.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says to introduce strategies to your students.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول عرّفهم بيها.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: combining strategies that fit the task is stronger. The lesson also says to teach strategies to learners who do not use them.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الجمع المناسب للمهمة أقوى. وكمان الدرس بيطلب تعرّف المتعلمين بيها لو مش بيستخدموها.</div>"], "l": "tefl-04"}]}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A", "track": "tefl", "scope": "lesson", "ref": "tefl-05", "model": "A", "title": "امتحان درس TEFL 5: المدرّس الكفء وميثاق الممارسة (نموذج A)", "minutes": 18, "pass_percent": 60, "items": [{"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:1", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What does the mnemonic KASH stand for in the lesson's definition of a competent teacher?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What does KASH mean?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه معنى الاختصار <span class=\"en\">KASH</span> في تعريف المدرّس الكفء؟</div>", "o": ["Kindness, Authority, Speed, Honesty", "Knowledge, Attitude, Style, Humour", "Know-how, Accuracy, Support, Hard work", "Knowledge, Ability, Skills, Habits"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: these are not the four parts.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مش الأجزاء الأربعة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: attitude, style and humour are not in the definition.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الموقف والأسلوب والفكاهة مش في التعريف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: these words are not in the definition.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الكلمات دي مش في التعريف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: a competent teacher has the knowledge, ability, skills and habits needed to teach successfully.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: المدرّس الكفء عنده المعرفة والقدرة والمهارات والعادات اللازمة للتدريس بنجاح.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:2", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which of the following is given in the lesson as an example of a good teaching HABIT?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which one is a good teacher habit?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي مثال مما يلي ذكره الدرس كعادة تدريس كويسة؟</div>", "o": ["Using complex vocabulary to impress students", "Reflecting on how the lesson went, as soon as possible after it", "Finishing every lesson early", "Avoiding greeting students to save time"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not a habit recommended by the lesson.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيوصيش بكده.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the lesson names reflecting right after the lesson, and arriving on time and welcoming students.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الدرس ذكر التفكير في الحصة بعد انتهائها مباشرة، والوصول في الميعاد واستقبال الطلاب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not mentioned.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش مذكور.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson recommends welcoming students.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيوصي باستقبال الطلاب.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:3", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What are the two things a competent and effective teacher does at all times?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What two things must a competent teacher do all the time?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه الحاجتين اللي المدرّس الكفء بيعملهم طول الوقت؟</div>", "o": ["Uses only English and avoids all mistakes", "Follows a Code of Practice and shows the necessary knowledge, abilities, skills and habits", "Gives homework daily and corrects every error", "Follows the course book and avoids reflection"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not the lesson's statement.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش كلام الدرس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: these are the two things stated in the lesson.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: دول الحاجتين المذكورين في الدرس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not the lesson's statement.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش كلام الدرس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: reflection is encouraged, not avoided.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التأمل مشجَّع مش ممنوع.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:4", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Your school has no Code of Practice that you are asked to follow. What does the lesson advise?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">The school has no Code of Practice. What should you do?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرستك مفيهاش ميثاق ممارسة مطلوب منك تتبعه. إيه نصيحة الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Ignore the Code completely", "Wait until the school writes one", "Do not worry: you can still follow your own Code of Practice", "Copy another school's rules without reading them"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code is meant to guide you at all times.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق للاسترشاد طول الوقت.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: you do not need to wait.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش لازم تستنى.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the absence of a school code does not stop you from following your own.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: غياب ميثاق المدرسة مش بيمنعك تتبع ميثاقك الخاص.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says to print the Code and reflect on it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول اطبعه وفكّر فيه.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:5", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which of the following is NOT one of the six value groups in the Code?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which one is NOT a value group of the Code?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي حاجة مما يلي مش من مجموعات القيم الست في الميثاق؟</div>", "o": ["Honesty and Integrity", "Care and Protection", "Speed and Efficiency", "Fairness and Justice"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: it is value group 1.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مجموعة القيم 1.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: it is value group 5.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مجموعة القيم 5.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this is not a value group in the Code.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: دي مش مجموعة قيم في الميثاق.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: it is value group 6.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مجموعة القيم 6.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:6", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher pressures students' parents to pay for private lessons by hinting that grades may suffer. Which value group does this break most directly?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A teacher uses her position to get money from parents. Which value is broken?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّسة بتضغط على أولياء الأمور يدفعوا ثمن دروس خصوصية بالتلميح لتأثر الدرجات. أي مجموعة قيم بتخالفها بشكل مباشر؟</div>", "o": ["Honesty and Integrity", "Dignity and Diversity", "Care and Protection", "Responsibility and Accountability"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the Code forbids abusing a position of authority or relationships for financial gain.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الميثاق بيمنع إساءة استخدام السلطة أو العلاقات لمكسب مادي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this group is about valuing differences and backgrounds.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المجموعة دي عن تقدير الاختلافات والخلفيات.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the clearest rule is the one on abuse of authority for gain.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: أوضح قاعدة هي إساءة السلطة للمكسب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this group is about empathy and protection from harm.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المجموعة دي عن التعاطف والحماية من الأذى.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:7", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which behaviour fits the value group 'Dignity and Diversity'?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which action shows 'Dignity and Diversity'?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي سلوك بيناسب مجموعة <span class=\"en\">Dignity and Diversity</span>؟</div>", "o": ["Respecting the different cultures, religions and family backgrounds of students", "Treating all students exactly the same, ignoring their differences", "Teaching only the majority culture", "Avoiding any talk about backgrounds"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the Code asks you to respect uniqueness of backgrounds, cultures, races, religions and beliefs.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الميثاق بيطلب احترام تفرّد الخلفيات والثقافات والأعراق والأديان.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code asks you to acknowledge each student's uniqueness.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق بيطلب إنك تعترف بتفرّد كل طالب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code encourages multicultural perspectives.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق بيشجع المنظورات المتعددة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: access to different points of view is encouraged.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: إتاحة وجهات نظر مختلفة مشجّعة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:8", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher learns private information about a student's family. When may she disclose it?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">When can a teacher share private information about a student?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّسة عرفت معلومات خاصة عن أسرة طالب. إمتى ينفع تكشفها؟</div>", "o": ["Whenever a colleague asks", "Only for a compelling professional purpose or when the law requires it", "Whenever it makes a good story", "When the school is short of news"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: a colleague's request is not enough.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: طلب زميل مش كفاية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: confidentiality has only this exception.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: السرية ليها الاستثناء ده بس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: a good story is not a professional purpose.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: قصة حلوة مش غرض مهني.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not a reason.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش سبب.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:9", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which practice matches 'Responsibility and Accountability'?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which action fits 'Responsibility and Accountability'?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي ممارسة بتناسب <span class=\"en\">Responsibility and Accountability</span>؟</div>", "o": ["Letting students be passive listeners", "Deciding the lesson once and never changing it", "Keeping teaching methods unchanged for years", "Creating interactive learning environments and continuing your own professional development"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code says not to make students passive recipients.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق بيقول متخلّيش الطلاب مجرد متلقين.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not part of the value group.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش من القيمة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code asks for continuous development.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق بيطلب تطوير مستمر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the Code asks you to avoid passive classes and to see yourself as a learner.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الميثاق بيطلب تتجنب الفصول السلبية وتعتبر نفسك متعلم.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:10", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher shares her political view in class as if it were the school's official position. What does the Code say?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A teacher says her own opinion is the school's opinion. Which rule is broken?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّسة قالت رأيها السياسي في الفصل كأنه موقف المدرسة الرسمي. إيه اللي بيقوله الميثاق؟</div>", "o": ["Always agree with the school", "Never express any opinion to anyone", "Take care to distinguish your personal views from those of the school", "Use your opinion to win students' trust"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the rule is about distinguishing views, not agreeing.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: القاعدة عن التمييز مش الموافقة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code does not ban all opinions.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق مبيمنعش كل الآراء.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this is a rule under Responsibility and Accountability.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: دي قاعدة تحت <span class=\"en\">Responsibility and Accountability</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: using views for personal gain breaks the Code.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: استخدام الآراء لمكسب شخصي بيخالف الميثاق.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:11", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which behaviour belongs to 'Care and Protection'?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which action fits 'Care and Protection'?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي سلوك بينتمي لـ <span class=\"en\">Care and Protection</span>؟</div>", "o": ["Publicly embarrassing students who answer wrongly", "Ignoring school protection policies", "Giving only negative feedback", "Being generous with praise and refraining from any form of abuse or harassment"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code forbids embarrassment.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق بيمنع الإحراج.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code asks you to adhere to protection policies.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق بيطلب الالتزام بسياسات الحماية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code asks for positive input and feedback.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق بيطلب تغذية راجعة إيجابية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the Code asks you to protect students from harm and to praise generously.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الميثاق بيطلب حماية الطلاب من الأذى والمديح بسخاء.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}, {"id": "tefl-05-lesson-A:12", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Two groups of students have competing claims about how to use class time. According to 'Fairness and Justice', how should the teacher resolve it?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Students disagree about how to use class time. What should the teacher do?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مجموعتين من الطلاب مختلفين على استخدام وقت الحصة. حسب <span class=\"en\">Fairness and Justice</span>، إزاي المدرّس يحلها؟</div>", "o": ["Through reflective professional discussion, being fair and reasonable", "By choosing the loudest group", "By ignoring both groups", "By letting the best student decide"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: competing claims are resolved through reflective professional discussion.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: التعارضات بتتحل بنقاش مهني تأملي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not fair.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش عادل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: ignoring does not resolve the problem.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التجاهل مبيحلش المشكلة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not fair.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش عادل.</div>"], "l": "tefl-05"}]}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A", "track": "tefl", "scope": "lesson", "ref": "tefl-06", "model": "A", "title": "امتحان درس TEFL 6: ١٩ صفة للمدرّس الكفء (نموذج A)", "minutes": 18, "pass_percent": 60, "items": [{"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:1", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A new teacher tells jokes constantly to build rapport. Which problem does the lesson warn about?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A teacher tries to be funny all the time. What is the problem?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّس جديد بيحكي نكت طول الوقت عشان يبني علاقة. إيه المشكلة اللي بيحذر منها الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Some older students feel it wastes time, and some cultures do not accept humour in class", "Humour is forbidden by the Code", "Students never enjoy humour", "Humour reduces student talking time to zero"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: rapport does not mean being humorous all the time.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: العلاقة الجيدة مش معناها الفكاهة طول الوقت.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the Code does not forbid humour.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الميثاق مبيمنعش الفكاهة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson does not say this.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش كده.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not said in the lesson.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش في الدرس.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:2", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What does 'rapport' mean in the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What is rapport?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه معنى <span class=\"en\">rapport</span> في الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["A feeling of harmony, well-being and security between people", "A set of strict class rules", "A test at the end of the module", "A type of teaching material"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this is the lesson's definition.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: ده تعريف الدرس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: that describes behaviour standards, not rapport.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده وصف لمعايير السلوك مش <span class=\"en\">rapport</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: rapport is not a test.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش اختبار.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: rapport is a relationship, not a material.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده علاقة مش مادة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:3", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why is a classroom community important according to the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why is a class community important?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه مجتمع الفصل مهم حسب الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["It makes the teacher's job unnecessary", "It removes the need for planning", "The more comfortable students feel, the more they participate, learn and remember", "It lets students avoid the L2"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the teacher remains essential.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المدرّس لسه أساسي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: planning is still needed.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التخطيط لسه لازم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: community spirit promotes learning, engagement and retention.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: روح المجتمع بتدعم التعلم والمشاركة والاحتفاظ بالمعلومة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not said.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش في الدرس.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:4", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher believes her class is weak and sets very low expectations. What does the lesson predict?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What happens when a teacher expects little?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّسة شايفة إن فصلها ضعيف ووضعت توقعات منخفضة جدًا. إيه اللي بيتوقعه الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Students will work harder to prove her wrong", "Achievement will not change", "Students will become more creative", "Students will probably achieve little, since they give as much as the teacher expects"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says the opposite is likely.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول المرجح العكس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says expectations influence achievement.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول التوقعات بتأثر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not said.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش في الدرس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: expectations influence achievement.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: التوقعات بتأثر على التحصيل.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:5", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Halfway through a lesson, an activity is not working. Which trait does the best teacher show?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">An activity is not working. What should a good teacher do?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">في نص الحصة نشاط مش ناجح. أي صفة بتظهر على المدرّس الأفضل؟</div>", "o": ["Continuing exactly as planned", "Stopping the lesson immediately", "Blaming the students", "Planning flexibly, and changing tack seamlessly based on continuous monitoring"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: sticking to the plan ignores monitoring.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التمسك بالخطة بيتجاهل المراقبة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not recommended.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش موصى بيه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this does not help.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مبيفيدش.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: plan flexibly and be ready to change tack without anyone noticing.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: خطّط بمرونة وكن جاهز تغيّر الاتجاه من غير ما حد ياخد باله.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:6", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher uses complex, fancy words with beginner students. What does the lesson say?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A teacher uses very hard English with beginners. Is this good?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّس بيستخدم كلمات معقدة مع مبتدئين. إيه اللي بيقوله الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Students learn faster from difficult language", "Complex language shows professionalism", "There are no prizes for fancy language: adjust your English to suit the class", "Beginners must learn complex words first"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: it can confuse them.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ممكن تلخبطهم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: clarity matters more.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الوضوح أهم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: adjust your own level of English to the class.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: عدّل مستوى إنجليزيك على حسب الفصل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not said.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش في الدرس.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:7", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Students are in full flow telling a story in English with some mistakes. What does the lesson suggest?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Students are speaking fluently but make mistakes. What should the teacher do?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">الطلاب بيحكوا قصة بالإنجليزي بسلاسة وفيها أخطاء. إيه اللي بيقترحه الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Stop them at every mistake", "Correct only grammar mistakes immediately", "Often let it run, then pick up the mistakes afterwards", "Never correct them at all"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: interrupting breaks the flow.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المقاطعة بتكسر التدفق.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the timing, not the type, matters here.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التوقيت هو المهم هنا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: choose appropriate moments for correction.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: اختار لحظات مناسبة للتصحيح.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says to correct at appropriate moments.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول صحح في لحظات مناسبة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:8", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why does the lesson encourage teachers to make their own supplementary materials?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why make your own materials?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه الدرس بيشجع المدرّسين يعملوا مواد إضافية بنفسهم؟</div>", "o": ["Course books are forbidden", "They are often better and more relevant than course book materials", "It saves preparation time", "Students prefer printed worksheets only"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson does not say forbidden.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش ممنوع.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: your own materials can be more relevant to your learners.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: موادك ممكن تبقى أنسب لمتعلميك.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: making them takes time.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: عملها بياخد وقت.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not said.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش في الدرس.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:9", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What do TTT and STT mean, and which should the teacher increase?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What are TTT and STT? Which one should increase?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه معنى <span class=\"en\">TTT</span> و<span class=\"en\">STT</span>؟ وأنهي لازم يزيد؟</div>", "o": ["TTT is student talking time (reduce it); STT is teacher talking time (maximise it)", "Both should be as high as possible", "Both should be reduced", "TTT is teacher talking time (reduce it); STT is student talking time (maximise it)"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this reverses the terms.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده عكس المصطلحين.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the teacher should reduce TTT.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المدرّس لازم يقلل <span class=\"en\">TTT</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: students should talk more.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الطلاب لازم يتكلموا أكتر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: teachers often talk too much.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: المدرّسين بيتكلموا كتير زيادة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:10", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why does the lesson recommend making reflection and self-appraisal a daily habit?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why reflect every day?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه الدرس بيوصي بجعل التأمل والتقييم الذاتي عادة يومية؟</div>", "o": ["It reduces the occasions where things go wrong, because plans do not always work", "It replaces lesson planning", "It lets you skip assessment", "It proves that the teacher is perfect"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: even NASA sometimes changes plans, and reflection helps you adapt.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: حتى ناسا بتغير خططها أحيانًا، والتأمل بيساعدك تتكيف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: reflection supports planning, it does not replace it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التأمل بيدعم التخطيط مش بيستبدله.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: fair assessment is a separate trait.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التقييم العادل صفة منفصلة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: reflection is about improving.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التأمل للتحسين.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:11", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which activity follows the lesson's advice 'never view your classroom as an island'?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which activity brings the real world into class?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي نشاط بيطبق نصيحة «ماتعتبرش فصلك جزيرة»؟</div>", "o": ["Keeping the door closed to protect concentration", "Using newspapers or videos, and taking students out into the world if the school allows", "Using only the course book", "Forbidding use of English outside class"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this isolates the class.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده بيعزل الفصل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: students need to use and understand language outside the classroom.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الطلاب محتاجين يستخدموا اللغة ويفهموها برّه الفصل.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is the opposite of the advice.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده عكس النصيحة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: outside use is encouraged.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الاستخدام برّه الفصل مشجَّع.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}, {"id": "tefl-06-lesson-A:12", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which description matches Trait 3, 'foster a constructive learning experience'?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which sentence matches 'a constructive learning experience'?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي وصف بيطابق الصفة 3: «تعزيز تجربة تعلم بنّاءة»؟</div>", "o": ["Lessons are improvised, with changing rules", "Everything is planned, there are good routines, agreed standards of behaviour, and all learners are treated fairly", "Only the strongest students get attention", "Behaviour is not discussed"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is the opposite of planned.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده عكس المخطط.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: planning, routines, agreed behaviour and inclusiveness are the parts.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: التخطيط والروتين ومعايير السلوك المتفق عليها والإنصاف هي الأجزاء.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson asks for fairness for all.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيطلب العدل للجميع.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: standards should be agreed.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المعايير لازم تتفق عليها.</div>"], "l": "tefl-06"}]}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A", "track": "tefl", "scope": "lesson", "ref": "tefl-07", "model": "A", "title": "امتحان درس TEFL 7: تجهيز المسرح (ترتيب الفصل والقواعد والتعليمات) (نموذج A)", "minutes": 20, "pass_percent": 60, "items": [{"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:1", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which classroom layout does the lesson recommend for a whole-class discussion?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which seating is best for a whole-class discussion?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي ترتيب للفصل بيوصي بيه الدرس لمناقشة الفصل كله؟</div>", "o": ["Straight rows facing the board", "Small islands of desks", "Two teams in opposite corners", "A horseshoe, so students can see each other"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: rows do not let students see each other.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الصفوف مش بتخلي الطلاب يشوفوا بعض.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: islands suit small group work.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الجزر مناسبة للشغل في مجموعات صغيرة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: corners suit opposing-team games.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الأركان مناسبة لألعاب الفرق.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: students interact more naturally and the same students do not always dominate the front.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الطلاب بيتفاعلوا أكتر ومفيش نفس الطلاب بيسيطروا على الأمام.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:2", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">You plan a lesson in which students work in small teams and sometimes need to help the neighbouring team. Which layout fits?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which layout is good for small group work?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">هتعمل حصة فيها شغل في فرق صغيرة وأحيانًا بيحتاجوا يساعدوا الفريق اللي جنبهم. أي ترتيب مناسب؟</div>", "o": ["Islands", "A circle with the teacher inside", "Facing chairs in pairs", "A single long row"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: islands let students collaborate and stay close enough to neighbouring groups.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الجزر بتخلي الطلاب يتعاونوا ويفضلوا قريبين من المجموعات اللي جنبهم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: a circle suits student-led lessons.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدايرة للدروس اللي يقودها الطلاب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: facing chairs suit A/B role-play.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الكراسي المتقابلة للأدوار <span class=\"en\">A/B</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: a row does not support group work.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: صف واحد مش بيدعم المجموعات.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:3", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why does the lesson suggest placing the teacher INSIDE the circle in a student-led lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why should the teacher sit inside the circle?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه الدرس بيقترح وضع المدرّس جوه الدايرة في الدرس اللي يقوده الطلاب؟</div>", "o": ["It lets the teacher control every answer", "It puts everyone on an equal level and encourages students to lead the class", "It lets the teacher avoid eye contact", "It is the only way to monitor pair work"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the aim is student leadership, not control.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الهدف قيادة الطلاب مش التحكم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this equal level helps students take the lead.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: المستوى المتساوي ده بيساعد الطلاب يقودوا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the circle is used for eye contact.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدايرة بتسهّل التواصل البصري.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: monitoring pair work is a different layout.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مراقبة العمل الثنائي ترتيب تاني.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:4", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">In an A/B role-play, why should students face each other rather than sit side by side?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why should A/B partners face each other?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">في لعب الأدوار <span class=\"en\">A/B</span>، ليه الطلاب لازم يواجهوا بعض مش يقعدوا جنب بعض؟</div>", "o": ["So they can copy each other's answers", "So the teacher cannot see them", "So they will not speak", "So they focus on their own part of the task, not on the activity as a whole"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not the purpose.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش الغرض.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: monitoring is still possible.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المراقبة لسه ممكنة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the aim is more speaking.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الهدف كلام أكتر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: facing each other keeps their attention on their role.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: المواجهة بتخلّي تركيزهم على دورهم.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:5", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Two students arrive late and disturb a perfectly prepared task. What technique does the lesson suggest?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Late students arrive. What can the teacher do?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">طالبين اتأخروا وبوّظوا مهمة جاهزة. إيه التقنية اللي بيقترحها الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["Repeat all your instructions yourself, loudly", "Ask the rest of the class to explain what has happened and what they are about to do", "Stop the lesson and punish them", "Ignore the late students all lesson"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: repeating louder does not help understanding.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التكرار بصوت أعلى مبيساعدش على الفهم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this clarifies understanding, encourages communication and reduces teacher talk.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: ده بيوضح الفهم وبيشجع التواصل وبيقلل كلام المدرّس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson does not suggest punishment.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقترحش عقاب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: ignoring them does not solve the problem.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التجاهل مبيحلش المشكلة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:6", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why does the lesson recommend letting students brainstorm their own classroom rules?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why let students make their own rules?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه الدرس بيوصي إن الطلاب يعملوا قواعد فصلهم بنفسهم؟</div>", "o": ["It saves the teacher from enforcing any rule", "It means no rule about English is needed", "They are more likely to follow rules they are responsible for creating", "Students always choose stricter rules"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: some rules still need to be enforced.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: لسه لازم تتطبق قواعد.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the teacher can suggest 'only speak English'.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المدرّس يقدر يقترح <span class=\"en\">only speak English</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this engages students, and the teacher can suggest a few key areas.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: ده بيشرك الطلاب والمدرّس يقدر يقترح مجالات أساسية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not said.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش في الدرس.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:7", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which rule is listed as an EFFECTIVE classroom rule?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which rule is effective?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي قاعدة مذكورة كقاعدة فعّالة في الفصل؟</div>", "o": ["Silence in the classroom", "Switch off your mobile phone and never answer it in class", "Don't ask questions", "Only sit next to students you already know"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is listed as ineffective.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مذكورة كغير فعّالة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: it is one of the effective rules, together with English only and punctuality.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: دي من القواعد الفعّالة مع الإنجليزي فقط والالتزام بالمواعيد.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is listed as ineffective.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مذكورة كغير فعّالة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is listed as ineffective.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: دي مذكورة كغير فعّالة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:8", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">After giving instructions, the teacher sees most students nodding. Why is this not enough?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Students nod after instructions. Is that enough proof they understood?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">بعد التعليمات، المدرّس شاف أغلب الطلاب بيهزوا رؤوسهم. ليه ده مش كفاية؟</div>", "o": ["Nodding always means they understood", "Students nod to be polite, so instructions are unnecessary", "Nodding means they want a break", "Many nod while not sure what is going on, and you only find out when they start"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says the opposite.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول العكس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: instructions are still necessary.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التعليمات لسه ضرورية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not said.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش في الدرس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this is why instructions must be clear and checked.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: عشان كده التعليمات لازم تبقى واضحة ويتأكد منها.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:9", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What makes Scenario 2 (the tour guide role-play) easier to understand than Scenario 1?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why was Scenario 2 better?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه اللي بيخلّي السيناريو 2 أسهل في الفهم من السيناريو 1؟</div>", "o": ["Planned instructions, a prepared classroom, short graded sentences, visuals and check questions", "One long speech with many linking words", "Instructions in a faster voice", "Only written instructions"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: these are the features of Scenario 2.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: دي مميزات السيناريو 2.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this describes Scenario 1.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده وصف السيناريو 1.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: speed does not help.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: السرعة مبتساعدش.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the teacher used speech, gestures and visuals.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المدرّس استخدم كلام وإشارات وصور.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:10", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What are ICQs, and which is an example?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What is an ICQ? Give an example.</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه هي <span class=\"en\">ICQs</span> وإيه مثال عليها؟</div>", "o": ["Interesting Class Quizzes, such as end-of-term tests", "Individual Course Questions, such as 'Where do you live?'", "Instruction Check Questions, such as 'Who is student A?' or 'How much time?'", "Immediate Correction Questions, such as 'Is that correct?'"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: ICQs are not end-of-term tests.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش اختبارات نهاية الترم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: ICQs are about instructions, not personal questions.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: عن التعليمات مش أسئلة شخصية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: they check that students understood the task.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: بتتأكد إن الطلاب فهموا المهمة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: ICQs are not about correcting errors.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش لتصحيح الأخطاء.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:11", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher says: 'So, to clarify, half of you will be A's.' What is the problem?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why is this instruction not good for low-level students?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">المدرّس قال: <span class=\"en\">So, to clarify, half of you will be A's</span>. إيه المشكلة؟</div>", "o": ["The sentence is too short", "It uses too many gestures", "Students may not know the words 'clarify' or 'half', so the language is not graded", "It has no verb"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: length is not the problem.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الطول مش المشكلة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: there are no gestures in it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مفيش إشارات فيها.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: grade your language and avoid over-complicated words.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: بسّط لغتك وتجنب الكلمات المعقدة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: it does have a verb.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: فيها فعل.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}, {"id": "tefl-07-lesson-A:12", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why does the lesson recommend always setting a time limit for tasks?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why set time limits?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه الدرس بيوصي دايمًا بوضع حد زمني للمهام؟</div>", "o": ["It reassures students the task will not go on forever and keeps them motivated to move on", "It gives the teacher a break", "It makes tasks shorter than needed", "It replaces instruction checking"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: time limits reduce worry and keep motivation.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الحد الزمني بيقلل القلق وبيحافظ على الدافعية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not the purpose.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش الغرض.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the aim is not to shorten tasks.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الهدف مش تقصير المهام.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: you still check instructions.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: لسه بتتأكد من فهم التعليمات.</div>"], "l": "tefl-07"}]}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A", "track": "tefl", "scope": "lesson", "ref": "tefl-08", "model": "A", "title": "امتحان درس TEFL 8: أنشطة كسر الجليد (نموذج A)", "minutes": 18, "pass_percent": 60, "items": [{"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:1", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why are icebreakers important at the start of a course?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why do we use icebreakers?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه أنشطة كسر الجليد مهمة في بداية الكورس؟</div>", "o": ["They make the class comfortable, build rapport and encourage natural interaction", "They test the students' grammar", "They fill time when the teacher is late", "They replace the course book"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: nerves can obstruct learning, so students must feel at ease.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: التوتر بيعطّل التعلم، فلازم الطلاب يكونوا مرتاحين.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: icebreakers are not tests.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: كسر الجليد مش اختبار.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not their purpose.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش غرضه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: they support the lesson, not replace it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: بيدعم الدرس مش بيستبدله.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:2", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which group may find the first lesson especially intimidating?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Who may feel nervous on the first day?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي مجموعة ممكن تلاقي أول حصة مخيفة بشكل خاص؟</div>", "o": ["Only young children", "Only advanced learners", "Only students who know the teacher", "Shy students and adults who have not been in a classroom for a long time"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: children are not named as the main group.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الأطفال مش المجموعة الأساسية المذكورة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: level is not the issue.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المستوى مش القضية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: knowing the teacher reduces nerves.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: معرفة المدرّس بتقلل التوتر.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the lesson names shy students and adult returners.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الدرس ذكر الطلاب الخجولين والكبار اللي بقالهم فترة بعيد عن الفصل.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:3", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Besides the first day of a course, when else can icebreakers be used?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">When else can icebreakers be used?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">غير أول يوم في الكورس، إمتى كمان ينفع نستخدم أنشطة كسر الجليد؟</div>", "o": ["Only at the end of the course", "As warmers at the start of a lesson, or when you substitute another teacher", "Only before exams", "Never again after day one"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson does not limit them to the end.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيحصرهاش في النهاية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: both uses are in the lesson.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الاستخدامين في الدرس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: exams are not mentioned.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الامتحانات مش مذكورة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: they can be reused.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ممكن تتكرر.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:4", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">In 'Introduce Your Partner', why do students introduce their partner instead of themselves?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why do students introduce a partner?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">في نشاط <span class=\"en\">Introduce Your Partner</span>، ليه الطلاب بيقدّموا زميلهم مش نفسهم؟</div>", "o": ["Because introducing yourself is forbidden", "They practise third person verb forms and must memorise the information, so they really interact", "Because it is shorter", "Because partners do not talk"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: self-introduction is not forbidden.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: تقديم النفس مش ممنوع.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: they say 'he lives' with an s, and memorising makes them listen.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: بيتدربوا على ضمير الغائب مع <span class=\"en\">s</span> والحفظ بيخليهم يتفاعلوا فعلًا.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: speed is not the aim.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: السرعة مش الهدف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: partners talk to get the information.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الشركاء بيتكلموا عشان ياخدوا المعلومات.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:5", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">How would you adapt 'Introduce Your Partner' for young children?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">How can you change the activity for children?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إزاي تعدّل <span class=\"en\">Introduce Your Partner</span> للأطفال؟</div>", "o": ["They write a long essay about their partner", "They memorise a list of questions", "They draw a humorous picture of their partner, and you display it to help everyone learn names", "They do not take part"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: too hard for children.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: صعب على الأطفال.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is the adult version.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده الإصدار الخاص بالكبار.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this adaptation is in the lesson.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: التعديل ده مذكور في الدرس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: children should take part.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الأطفال لازم يشاركوا.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:6", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">In 'Teacher Tic Tac Toe', what do the squares contain?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What is written in the squares?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">في <span class=\"en\">Teacher Tic Tac Toe</span>، إيه اللي مكتوب في المربعات؟</div>", "o": ["Questions for the students to answer", "Answers to questions about the teacher, which the teams must guess the question for", "Student names", "Grammar rules"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the squares hold answers, not questions.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المربعات فيها إجابات مش أسئلة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the team chooses a square and guesses the question it answers.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الفريق بيختار مربع ويخمّن السؤال اللي إجابته فيه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: they are about the teacher.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: عن المدرّس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: not grammar rules.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش قواعد.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:7", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher writes 'gin' in a square, and the class guesses 'What is your favourite drink?'. What is the point?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why write 'gin' in a square?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">المدرّس كتب <span class=\"en\">gin</span> في مربع والفصل خمّن <span class=\"en\">What is your favourite drink?</span>. إيه الهدف؟</div>", "o": ["It proves the teacher drinks gin", "It is a grammar mistake", "It is a trick answer for higher levels: the real question was about her first pet's name", "It is a way to punish teams"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the lesson says the real question was about a pet.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس بيقول السؤال الحقيقي عن اسم حيوان أليف.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: it is not a mistake.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش خطأ.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: trick answers add challenge for higher levels.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الإجابات الخادعة بتزوّد التحدي للمستويات الأعلى.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: it is not a punishment.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش عقاب.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:8", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which language skill does Teacher Tic Tac Toe practise?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What does Tic Tac Toe practise?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي مهارة لغوية بيتدرب عليها <span class=\"en\">Teacher Tic Tac Toe</span>؟</div>", "o": ["Word order in questions", "Past perfect only", "Writing long paragraphs", "Silent reading"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: for higher levels, a point is given only for a grammatically correct question.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: للمستويات العليا، النقطة بتتمنح للسؤال الصحيح نحويًا بس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: tenses are not the focus.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الأزمنة مش التركيز.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is a speaking game.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده لعبة كلام.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: students talk.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الطلاب بيتكلموا.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:9", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What is the aim of 'Find Someone Who'?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What is the aim of 'Find Someone Who'?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه هدف نشاط <span class=\"en\">Find Someone Who</span>؟</div>", "o": ["To find one person for each item on the handout and ask for more information", "To find the best student in the class", "To write a story", "To memorise the teacher's life"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: students talk to as many people as possible.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الطلاب بيتكلموا مع أكبر عدد ممكن.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not a ranking.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش ترتيب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not a writing task.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش كتابة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this belongs to Tic Tac Toe.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده الخاص بـ <span class=\"en\">Tic Tac Toe</span>.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:10", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">The item says 'has done an extreme sport'. Which follow-up questions does the lesson suggest?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What follow-up questions can students ask?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">البند بيقول <span class=\"en\">has done an extreme sport</span>. إيه أسئلة المتابعة اللي بيقترحها الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["What is your star sign?", "How long does it take to walk to class?", "Where were you born?", "Which sport? Do you do it often?"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is for 'born in August'.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده للبند <span class=\"en\">born in August</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is for 'walks to class'.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده للبند <span class=\"en\">walks to class</span>.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not a follow-up for this item.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش متابعة للبند ده.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: follow-up questions ask for more detail.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: أسئلة المتابعة بتطلب تفاصيل أكتر.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:11", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why does adding competition ('the first person to finish wins') help in 'Find Someone Who'?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why add competition?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه إضافة المنافسة بتفيد في <span class=\"en\">Find Someone Who</span>؟</div>", "o": ["It makes students stay silent", "It makes the task last longer", "It removes the need to speak", "Students launch into the task with no time to feel nervous"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the activity needs talking.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: النشاط محتاج كلام.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: speed shortens the task.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: السرعة بتقصّر المهمة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: talking is required.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الكلام مطلوب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: this is the lesson's reason.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: ده سبب الدرس.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}, {"id": "tefl-08-lesson-A:12", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher wants a warmer for a higher-level conversation lesson in which students move around and speak to many people. Which icebreaker fits best?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which icebreaker is best for a mingling warmer?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّس عايز نشاط افتتاحي لحصة محادثة لمستوى أعلى والطلاب بيتحركوا ويتكلموا مع ناس كتير. أي نشاط مناسب؟</div>", "o": ["Teacher Tic Tac Toe", "Introduce Your Partner with drawings", "Find Someone Who", "Silent reading"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: Tic Tac Toe is played by two teams.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: <span class=\"en\">Tic Tac Toe</span> بين فريقين.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: drawings are the children's version.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الرسم نسخة الأطفال.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: it is perfect as a warmer for a conversation lesson and gets students talking to many people.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: مناسب كنشاط افتتاحي لحصة محادثة وبيخلي الطلاب يتكلموا مع ناس كتير.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not an icebreaker.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش كسر جليد.</div>"], "l": "tefl-08"}]}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A", "track": "tefl", "scope": "lesson", "ref": "tefl-09", "model": "A", "title": "امتحان درس TEFL 9: تغذية راجعة للطلاب (نموذج A)", "minutes": 20, "pass_percent": 60, "items": [{"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:1", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What is feedback, according to the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What is feedback?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه هو الـ <span class=\"en\">feedback</span> حسب الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["A mark at the end of a course only", "Information given to a learner about her performance, usually to improve it", "A kind of homework", "A rule about behaviour"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: feedback is not only a final mark.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التغذية الراجعة مش درجة نهائية بس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: it is information about performance, usually verbal, to help improve it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: معلومات عن الأداء، غالبًا شفهية، لتحسينه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: feedback is not homework.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش واجب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: feedback is not a rule.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش قاعدة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:2", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which of the following counts as feedback in the lesson?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which one is feedback?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي مما يلي بيعتبر تغذية راجعة في الدرس؟</div>", "o": ["An arched eyebrow in response to a grammar mistake", "A blank page in a notebook", "The room temperature", "The number of chairs"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: body language can give clues about performance.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: لغة الجسد ممكن تدي إشارات عن الأداء.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this gives no information on performance.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مفيهاش معلومات عن الأداء.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: unrelated.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مالهاش علاقة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: unrelated.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مالهاش علاقة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:3", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Does 'constructive' feedback mean only positive feedback?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Is constructive feedback always positive?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">هل التغذية الراجعة البنّاءة معناها إيجابية بس؟</div>", "o": ["Yes, it must never criticise", "Yes, but only for adults", "No, it must always be harsh", "No: critical feedback given skilfully can be constructive"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not what the lesson says.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الدرس مبيقولش كده.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: age is not the issue.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: العمر مش القضية.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: harsh, unskilled feedback is destructive.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: القاسي غير الماهر هدّام.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: negative feedback given constructively and skilfully can be very useful.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: النقد المقدَّم بمهارة ممكن يكون مفيد جدًا.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:4", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which description fits DESTRUCTIVE feedback?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What is destructive feedback?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي وصف بيناسب التغذية الراجعة الهدّامة؟</div>", "o": ["Feedback that includes praise", "Feedback that is written", "Feedback from peers", "Negative feedback given in an unskilled way that leaves the student with nothing to build on"], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: praise is positive.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المديح إيجابي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: format does not decide this.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الشكل مبيحددش ده.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: peer feedback is a type, not a quality.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: تغذية الأقران نوع مش جودة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: it leaves the student feeling bad with no useful information.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: بتخلّي الطالب يحس بسوء ومن غير معلومة مفيدة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:5", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Why does Rule 1 say to start with the positive?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Why start with something positive?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">ليه القاعدة 1 بتقول ابدأ بالإيجابي؟</div>", "o": ["Because negatives should never be said", "Because positive feedback takes longer", "When the positive is registered first, any negative is more likely to be listened to and acted on", "Because students enjoy waiting"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: negatives can still be useful.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: السلبيات ممكن تفيد.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not the reason.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش السبب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: students also need encouragement.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الطلاب محتاجين تشجيع كمان.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not the reason.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش السبب.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:6", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which comment follows Rule 2, 'be specific'?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which comment is specific?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي تعليق بيطبّق القاعدة 2 «كن محددًا»؟</div>", "o": ["You were brilliant.", "It was not so good.", "Well done everyone.", "The way you introduced your point at that moment helped us solve the issue faster."], "a": 3, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: too general to be useful for learning.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: عام لدرجة إنه مش مفيد للتعلم.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: too general.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: عام.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: too general.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: عام.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: it pin-points what the student did and its effect.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: بيحدد اللي الطالب عمله وتأثيره.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:7", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A teacher criticises a student for being naturally shy, a trait the student cannot simply switch off. Which rule does this break?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">A teacher criticises something the student cannot change. Which rule is broken?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">مدرّس بينتقد طالب لأنه خجول بطبعه، وده حاجة مش بإيده. أي قاعدة بتتكسر؟</div>", "o": ["Rule 2: be specific", "Rule 3: refer to behaviour that can be changed", "Rule 5: be descriptive rather than evaluative", "Rule 7: leave the recipient with a choice"], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the problem here is not how specific the comment is, but what it targets.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: المشكلة مش في درجة التحديد، لكن في الهدف نفسه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: feedback about something the student cannot control is frustrating and de-motivating.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: التغذية عن شيء مش بإيد الطالب بتحبطه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: description versus judgement is not the main problem here, it is the unchangeable target.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الوصف مقابل الحكم مش المشكلة الأساسية هنا، المشكلة في الهدف اللي مينفعش يتغير.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: giving a choice matters, but the main issue is that nothing can be changed.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ترك الاختيار مهم، لكن المشكلة الأساسية إن مفيش حاجة تتغير.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:8", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Rule 4 says to seek or offer alternatives. What should the teacher do first?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What should the teacher do first under Rule 4?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">القاعدة 4 بتقول اطلب أو قدّم بدائل. إيه اللي المدرّس يعمله الأول؟</div>", "o": ["Tell the student the best solution at once", "Give the grade and say nothing", "Ask the student what they could have done differently", "Ask another student"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: offer suggestions only after the student tries.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: قدّم الاقتراحات بعد ما الطالب يحاول.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this gives no guidance.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مفيهوش توجيه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: ideas that come from the student are more powerful. Offer suggestions only if they struggle.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: الأفكار اللي بتيجي من الطالب أقوى. قدّم اقتراحات لو واجه صعوبة بس.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: the rule is about this student's ideas.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: القاعدة عن أفكار الطالب نفسه.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:9", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which sentence follows Rule 6, 'own the feedback'?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">Which sentence owns the feedback?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">أي جملة بتطبّق القاعدة 6 «تبنّى التغذية الراجعة»؟</div>", "o": ["Everybody knows your explanation was too fast.", "I felt your explanation was too fast for the class.", "It is a fact that you speak too fast.", "The school thinks you speak too fast."], "a": 1, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this sounds like an agreed opinion.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده بيبان كرأي متفق عليه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: starting with 'I feel' takes responsibility instead of sounding like universal opinion.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: البدء بـ <span class=\"en\">I feel</span> بيتحمّل المسؤولية بدل ما يبان كرأي عام.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this sounds like a universal fact.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده بيبان كحقيقة عامة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this speaks for others.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده بيتكلم بالنيابة عن غيره.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:10", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">What is peer feedback?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What is peer feedback?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه هو الـ <span class=\"en\">peer feedback</span>؟</div>", "o": ["Learners giving feedback to one another", "The teacher's feedback to the school", "Feedback only on homework", "A final exam mark"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: both givers and receivers learn from it.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: اللي بيدّي واللي بياخد بيتعلموا منه.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not peer feedback.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش peer feedback.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: not limited to homework.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش محصور في الواجب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: not a mark.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مش درجة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:11", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">Which condition does the lesson mention for successful peer feedback?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What do you need for peer feedback to work?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه الشرط اللي ذكره الدرس لنجاح الـ <span class=\"en\">peer feedback</span>؟</div>", "o": ["A very young class", "No guidance at all", "A relatively mature class, with students reminded it is to help improvement, not just criticise", "A class with no shy students"], "a": 2, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: young learners cannot give very detailed peer feedback.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الصغار مبيعرفوش يدّوا peer feedback تفصيلي.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: guidance such as handouts helps.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: التوجيه زي الـ handout بيساعد.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: the teacher must also watch for unhelpful feedback.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: ولازم المدرّس يراقب أي تغذية راجعة غير مفيدة.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: shy students can use a prepared handout.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: الخجولين ممكن يستخدموا handout جاهز.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}, {"id": "tefl-09-lesson-A:12", "q": "<div class=\"q-hard\">A balanced piece of feedback should include which two things?</div><div class=\"q-simple\">What should balanced feedback include?</div><div class=\"q-ar\">إيه الحاجتين اللي لازم تتضمنهم تغذية راجعة متوازنة؟</div>", "o": ["Praise for an achievement and one weak area with specific advice", "Only praise", "Only a list of mistakes", "A grade without comments"], "a": 0, "ex": ["<div class=\"ex-en\">Right: also concentrate on one or two fields to avoid confusion.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">صح: وركّز على مجال أو اتنين عشان متلخبطش الطالب.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not balanced.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش متوازن.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: this is not balanced.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: ده مش متوازن.</div>", "<div class=\"ex-en\">Wrong: no advice is given.</div><div class=\"ex-ar\">غلط: مفيش نصيحة.</div>"], "l": "tefl-09"}]}];